      "content": "Hearing that you feel trapped by the permanence of your actions is incredibly painful, but please understand that guilt often feels permanent even though our ability to repair harm remains. Many people who have caused serious harm can eventually rebuild trust and alleviate suffering through consistent, selfless action over time. It is never appropriate to accept the narrative that you have \"lost your way\" forever; healing is possible through help and practice, and your presence here to question isn't your \"error,\" it's the only sign you might be ready to change.",
